    "theory": {
      "summary": "The iconic opening Largo of Chopin's Ballade No. 1: a grand unison octave arpeggio on the Neapolitan 6th (Ab/C = bII6) resolving into G minor.",
      "pattern_tip": "Hear Bars 1-3 as a single giant Ab-major triad in first inversion (C-Eb-Ab-C-Eb-Ab-C) before the dramatic Eb -> D sigh over D7.",
      "technique_tip": "Shape the rising octave arpeggio with deep, unhurried arm weight and listen carefully to the poignant silence into the G-minor resolution.",
      "ballade_link": "Direct study of Op. 23 mm. 1-7: bII6 (Neapolitan 6th) -> V7 -> i."
    }
  },
